# Pack-product host (law)

Read skill **forja-pack-product-host** when deciding pack vs host vs foundation, editing the kit painter, or `open.surface` routing.

**One-liner:** Empty shell + engines. Packs are product. Foundation paints only. Host validates + paints pack JSON — never invents product fields or verbs.

### Sniff tests

| Layer | Test |
|-------|------|
| **Host** | Pack uninstalled — does this Dart still make sense as a **generic** capability? No → pack (or delete) |
| **Foundation** | shadcn-style props in → UI out? Else host engine or pack |
| **Painter** | Names schedule/feed/panel/tabs or invents `title`/`poster` heuristics? Illegal — validate props → DS mount only |

### Hard forbidden (summary)

- Product folders / pack-id branches / hub inventory in `apps/forja`
- Field mappers (`title`/`poster`/`homeTeam`) or product runtimes in host
- Orchestrators / hooks / registries in `forja_foundation`
- Painter branches on product verbs (`feed`/`layout`/`rail`)
- Assert shipped pack ids in host tests

